course: dictionary
lesson: 4096
title: Ginger: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which one is meant. Ginger can be a spicy root, a colour, or a word people use for someone with red hair. «Many pigs are pink, but many breeds are black, spotted, ginger or hairy» uses ginger as a colour, because the other words in the list are all ways a pig can look.
explain: Now look at «a ginger cat». Here ginger is a colour word, so it means orange-brown. In «ginger biscuits», the word means the spicy root that goes into cooking. The words after ginger tell you which meaning to choose.
explain: Always check by swapping in your meaning. Does «ginger cat» still make sense if you think of it as a spicy root? No. So you have your answer.
fact: Ginger is a plant root with a hot, spicy taste, used in cooking and drinks.
fact: As an adjective, ginger means orange-brown, especially for hair or a cat's fur.
fact: «Ginger beer» and «ginger ale» are fizzy drinks made with ginger.
fact: Informal UK slang uses «a ginger» for a person with red or orange hair, and it can be unkind, so think about how it may feel to the person.
fact: In French, ginger hair is roux or rousse, never rouge, which means red.
exercise: «The chef grated fresh ginger into the stir-fry.» What is ginger in this sentence? | A small orange cat | A pink farm animal | A child with red hair | *A plant root with a hot, spicy taste
exercise: «The ginger cat slept on the warm windowsill.» What colour is the cat? | Black | Blue-grey | *Orange-brown | Bright pink
exercise: «The ginger tom ran up the tree.» Find and copy the word that tells you the colour of the tom. | ran | tree | tom | *ginger
test: «Ginger beer is fizzy and sweet.» What is ginger beer? | A cat with orange fur | A stir-fry with spices | *A fizzy drink made with ginger | A beer made from wild boar
test: Why might someone feel upset if called a ginger? | Because it means they are very old | Because it is the name of a spicy sauce | *Because it can be an unkind word for red or orange hair | Because ginger is a sad colour
exam: In «Pigs can be pink, black, ginger, spotted», what does ginger mean? | A spicy root for cooking | *The colour orange-brown | A child with red hair | A fizzy drink
